A prominent case is an escaped continuation after a comma, colon or
semicolon. Quotes, brackets and math/Markdown delimiters also give pulses. Joins inside one token are generally weaker than joins across tokens;
spaces and blank lines weaken many of them. Closing quotes are stronger
when their opening quote is recent; middle-dot leaders also give a negative
pulse. Ordinary text stays near zero.
