    return (doc, token, (history + token)[-100:]), value

"""Contextual function words in multilingual text.

Completed words vote for English or another language using dictionary frequencies.
With non-English context, articles and prepositions from other languages get a
positive response; English function-word-shaped tokens get a negative response.
An immediately preceding English-looking word weakens that negative response.
Votes fade with each word and reset at document IDs or end-of-text markers.
Articles are weaker after prepositions, especially in the phrase "de la".
Greek article pieces and middle-dot separators have small additional rules.
In kana-rich text, frequent Chinese spellings get a weak negative response.
"""
from functools import lru_cache
import math
