"""A document-onset pulse, prolonged by repetition of the opening token.

The initial contribution is usually negative. Words, indentation, and empty
line comments give larger negative pulses than digits or plain punctuation.
An opening run of middle-dot pairs is particularly negative. After the run
ends, predict a small positive transient fading to a near-zero background.
These shape rules omit most word-specific fluctuations.
