Full, lowercase English words respond most reliably. Capitalized forms,
word fragments and code identifiers are weaker. Other languages' common
copulas also respond. Recent words' corpus frequencies disambiguate foreign
spellings; the previous word helps with English pronouns and contracted 's.
Unlisted tokens get zero; contracted 've and 'd get small negative values.
